From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: preserve an assembler-provided Merkle root in prepared
 blocks

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Update BlockAssembler::CreateNewBlock to assemble block templates from
the speculative Merklix overlay.

Original-Commit: ec16338243bb4554435e96084ad95bad25639b5a
Original-Patch: ecash/008
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.
---
 src/test/util/mining.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/test/util/mining.cpp b/src/test/util/mining.cpp
index 44da1beba8c002e4461bedd5824ab23c32ebb366..b60095383a8470245278a6dc02ca0d32570f90a0 100644
--- a/src/test/util/mining.cpp
+++ b/src/test/util/mining.cpp
@@ -61,7 +61,9 @@ PrepareBlock(const Config &config, const NodeContext &node,
 
     LOCK(cs_main);
     block->nTime = Assert(node.chainman)->ActiveTip()->GetMedianTimePast() + 1;
-    block->hashMerkleRoot = BlockMerkleRoot(*block);
+    if (block->hashMerkleRoot.IsNull()) {
+        block->hashMerkleRoot = BlockMerkleRoot(*block);
+    }
 
     return block;
 }
